IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa20-part26.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 26 (Arrangements and reconstructions: general), ss 895 to 901,
-- lines 12203-12331 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (coa20's range is 12203-13131: Parts 26, 26A and 27).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE ("the text says no in its own
-- words") or NOTHING ("not covered"); a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Each branch that answers no carries
-- -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"   and each branch that answers not covered carries
-- -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)   (silent / list not closed / includes / undefined term / points outside the text / limited by its own wording).
-- Seams (inputs another part answers) are named for the answering section, e.g. `s 1121 the officer is in default`.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.

-- ===========================================================================================================
-- SHARED NOUNS AND HELPERS of this subject's Parts 26, 26A and 27 (every name begins with a section label)
-- ===========================================================================================================

-- Who may apply to the court (ss 896(2), 899(2), 901C(2), 901F(3), 938(2) all use the same list of applicants).
DECLARE `s 896(2) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 896(2) the company`
    `s 896(2) a creditor of the company`
    `s 896(2) a member of the company`
    `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company`
    `s 896(2) the administrator of the company`
    `s 896(2) any other person`

-- Who an offence of default can be charged against (ss 897(5), 901D(5)): the company, an officer in default, or a person
-- the section treats as an officer (a liquidator or administrator, or a trustee of a deed securing debentures).
DECLARE `s 897(5) person charged with the default` IS ONE OF
    `s 897(5) the company`
    `s 897(5) an officer of the company`
    `s 897(5) a liquidator or administrator of the company`
    `s 897(5) a trustee of a deed for securing the issue of debentures of the company`
    `s 897(5) any other person`

-- Penalties. The core's `Penalty` and `Fine limit` carry them; the pounds a level or the statutory maximum stands for are not in the Act.
-- A conviction "on summary conviction" in general words covers a summary conviction in each of the three places.
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 897(8) the conviction is a summary conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      limit IS A `Fine limit`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` MEANS
    Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST limit, NOTHING, FALSE

GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      limit IS A `Fine limit`
      daily IS A `Fine limit`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 900(8) a penalty of a fine and a daily default fine for continued contravention` MEANS
    Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST limit, JUST daily, FALSE

-- Three-valued disjunction used where a section says "subject to" several others: JUST TRUE if any answers JUST TRUE;
-- JUST FALSE if all answer JUST FALSE; otherwise NOTHING (some answer is not covered and none says yes).
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST TRUE) answers
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING answers
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer the caller could not give is not turned into a no
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every provision consulted answered no

-- The three states of a requirement that a section imposes and another section may switch off (Part 27 uses this throughout).
DECLARE `s 903(1) status of a requirement` IS ONE OF
    `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
    `s 903(1) requirement not complied with`
    `s 903(1) requirement does not apply`
    `s 903(1) requirement not covered`

-- excluded: the answer of the sections that switch the requirement off (JUST TRUE = switched off, JUST FALSE = not, NOTHING = not known).
-- complied: whether the facts the requirement asks for are in order. A requirement that is switched off is not asked for.
GIVEN excluded IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      complied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 903(1) the status of the requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER excluded
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply" (the excluding section says so)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 903(1) requirement not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an excluding section applies is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF complied
        THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
        ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (2026-11-05 ruling: decided here, fork F3)

-- A calendar month later than a date: the library's `add months` clamps the day (31 January + 1 month = 28 or 29 February).
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 906(3) the date one month after` MEANS `add months` date 1

-- The same, backwards: the date one month before a date (31 March - 1 month = 28 or 29 February).
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 906(3) the date one month before` MEANS `add months` date (0 MINUS 1)

-- ===========================================================================================================
§ `Part 26 -- Arrangements and reconstructions: general`
-- ===========================================================================================================

§§ `Application of this Part (s 895)`

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing the scope of the Part)
-- src:12206 | (1) The provisions of this Part apply where a compromise or arrangement is proposed between a company and—
-- src:12207 | (a) its creditors, or any class of them, or
-- src:12208 | (b) its members, or any class of them.
@ref s 895(1) The Part applies where a compromise or arrangement is proposed with creditors or members (src:12206-12208)
GIVEN `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its members, or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 895(1) the provisions of Part 26 apply` MEANS
    IF `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of them`
       OR `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its members, or any class of them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this Part apply where a compromise or arrangement is proposed between a company and"

-- JURAL none (a definition)
-- src:12209 | (2) In this Part—
-- src:12210 | “arrangement” includes a reorganisation of the company's share capital by the consolidation of shares of different classes or by the division of shares into shares of different classes, or by both of those methods; and
@ref s 895(2) "arrangement" includes a reorganisation of the share capital (src:12209-12210)
GIVEN `by the consolidation of shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by the division of shares into shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 895(2) the reorganisation of the share capital is an arrangement` MEANS
    IF `by the consolidation of shares of different classes` OR `by the division of shares into shares of different classes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“arrangement” includes a reorganisation of the company's share capital by the consolidation of shares of different classes or by the division of shares into shares of different classes, or by both"

DECLARE `s 895(2) place where the word company is used` IS ONE OF
    `s 895(2) in section 900`
    `s 895(2) elsewhere in Part 26`

-- JURAL none (a definition)
-- src:12211 | “company”—
-- src:12212 | (a) in section 900 (powers of court to facilitate reconstruction or amalgamation) means a company within the meaning of this Act, and
-- src:12213 | (b) elsewhere in this Part means any company liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 895(2) "company" in s 900 and elsewhere in Part 26 (src:12211-12213)
GIVEN place IS A `s 895(2) place where the word company is used`
      `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 895(2) the body is a company for the purposes of Part 26` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 895(2) in section 900` THEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` -- the definition is "means a company within the meaning of this Act": the seam answer (JUST FALSE is its "means" no)
    WHEN `s 895(2) elsewhere in Part 26` THEN `the body is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` -- "means any company liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 ...": a borrowed definition, supplied as an input (NOTHING = not known)

-- JURAL none (a rule of precedence between Parts)
-- src:12214 | (3) The provisions of this Part have effect subject to Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) where that Part applies (see sections 902 and 903).
@ref s 895(3) Part 26 has effect subject to Part 27 where that Part applies (src:12214)
GIVEN `s 902(1) this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 895(3) the provisions of Part 26 have effect subject to Part 27` MEANS
    IF `s 902(1) this Part applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) where that Part applies"

§§ `Court order for holding of meeting (s 896)`

-- JURAL the creditors or members concerned: liability to be summoned to a meeting | the court: power (s 896(1)); the applicant: power to apply | the court: liability to hear it (s 896(2))
-- src:12217 | (1) The court may, on an application under this section, order a meeting of the creditors or class of creditors, or of the members of the company or class of members (as the case may be), to be summoned in such manner as the court directs.
@ref s 896(1) The court may, on an application, order a meeting (src:12217)
GIVEN `an application under section 896 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 896(1) the court may order a meeting of the creditors, class of creditors, members or class of members` MEANS
    IF `an application under section 896 has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on an application under this section"

-- src:12218 | (2) An application under this section may be made by—
-- src:12219 | (a) the company,
-- src:12220 | (b) any creditor or member of the company,
-- src:12221 | (c) if the company is being wound up, the liquidator, or
-- src:12222 | (d) if the company is in administration, the administrator.
@ref s 896(2) Who may apply for the order (src:12218-12222)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 896(2) applicant`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 896(2) the person may apply for an order for a meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 896(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is being wound up, the liquidator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F26)
    WHEN `s 896(2) the administrator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is in administration` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is in administration, the administrator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F26)
    WHEN `s 896(2) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An application under this section may be made by" lists, and does not say "only"

-- JURAL the company (a corporation that is a creditor): power to appoint a representative | the meeting: liability to receive that representative (s 323 is outside this range)
-- src:12223 | (3) Section 323 (representation of corporations at meetings) applies to a meeting of creditors under this section as to a meeting of the company (references to a member of the company being read as references to a creditor).
@ref s 896(3) Section 323 applies to a meeting of creditors under this section (src:12223)
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting of creditors under section 896` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 896(3) section 323 applies to the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a meeting of creditors under section 896`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a meeting of creditors under this section"

-- JURAL none (a signpost whose effect is s 899A)
-- src:12224 | (4) This section is subject to section 899A (moratorium debts, etc).
@ref s 896(4) This section is subject to section 899A (src:12224)
GIVEN `s 899A(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 896(4) section 896 is subject to section 899A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 899A(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 899A does not apply, and s 896(4) says nothing else
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 899A applies is not known

§§ `Statement to be circulated or made available (s 897)`

DECLARE `s 897(1) how a notice summoning the meeting is given` IS ONE OF
    `s 897(1) sent to a creditor or member`
    `s 897(1) given by advertisement`

-- JURAL the creditor or member: claim to the statement | the company: duty to send it (s 897(1)(a))
-- src:12226 | (1) Where a meeting is summoned under section 896—
-- src:12227 | (a) every notice summoning the meeting that is sent to a creditor or member must be accompanied by a statement complying with this section, and
-- src:12228 | (b) every notice summoning the meeting that is given by advertisement must either—
-- src:12229 | (i) include such a statement, or
-- src:12230 | (ii) state where and how creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting may obtain copies of such a statement.
@ref s 897(1) The notice must be accompanied by, or give access to, a statement (src:12226-12230)
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 896` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `s 897(1) how a notice summoning the meeting is given`
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement complying with section 897` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advertisement includes such a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advertisement states where and how creditors or members entitled to attend may obtain copies of such a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 897(1) the notice summoning the meeting satisfies the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a meeting is summoned under section 896`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a meeting is summoned under section 896" (the requirement does not arise)
    ELSE CONSIDER how
         WHEN `s 897(1) sent to a creditor or member` THEN
             IF `the notice is accompanied by a statement complying with section 897`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a statement complying with this section" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)
         WHEN `s 897(1) given by advertisement` THEN
             IF `the advertisement includes such a statement` OR `the advertisement states where and how creditors or members entitled to attend may obtain copies of such a statement`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must either— (i) include such a statement, or (ii) state where and how"

-- JURAL the company: duty to explain | the creditors and members: claim to the explanation (s 897(2)); interests of directors: duty of disclosure | the company (s 897(2)(b))
-- src:12231 | (2) The statement must—
-- src:12232 | (a) explain the effect of the compromise or arrangement, and
-- src:12233 | (b) in particular, state—
-- src:12234 | (i) any material interests of the directors of the company (whether as directors or as members or as creditors of the company or otherwise), and
-- src:12235 | (ii) the effect on those interests of the compromise or arrangement, in so far as it is different from the effect on the like interests of other persons.
@ref s 897(2) What the statement must explain and state (src:12231-12235)
GIVEN `the statement explains the effect of the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states any material interests of the directors of the company (whether as directors or as members or as creditors of the company or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states the effect on those interests of the compromise or arrangement, in so far as it is different from the effect on the like interests of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 897(2) the statement complies` MEANS
    IF `the statement explains the effect of the compromise or arrangement`
       AND `the statement states any material interests of the directors of the company (whether as directors or as members or as creditors of the company or otherwise)`
       AND `the statement states the effect on those interests of the compromise or arrangement, in so far as it is different from the effect on the like interests of other persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must— (a) explain the effect of the compromise or arrangement, and (b) in particular, state"

-- src:12236 | (3) Where the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders of the company, the statement must give the like explanation as respects the trustees of any deed for securing the issue of the debentures as it is required to give as respects the company's directors.
@ref s 897(3) Debenture holders: the like explanation as respects the trustees (src:12236)
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the like explanation as respects the trustees of any deed for securing the issue of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 897(3) the statement complies as respects debenture holders` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders" (the text requires nothing here otherwise)
    ELSE IF `the statement gives the like explanation as respects the trustees of any deed for securing the issue of the debentures`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the statement must give the like explanation as respects the trustees"

-- JURAL the creditor or member entitled to attend: claim to a free copy | the company: duty to provide it
-- src:12237 | (4) Where a notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting, every such creditor or member is entitled, on making application in the manner indicated by the notice, to be provided by the company with a copy of the statement free of charge.
@ref s 897(4) A creditor or member may have a copy of the statement free of charge (src:12237)
GIVEN `the notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied in the manner indicated by the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 897(4) the person is entitled to be provided by the company with a copy of the statement free of charge` MEANS
    IF `the notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting`
       AND `the person is a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting`
       AND `the person has applied in the manner indicated by the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a notice given by advertisement states ... every such creditor or member is entitled, on making application in the manner indicated by the notice"

-- The offence of default: the company, and every officer of the company who is in default, subject to subsection (7).
-- JURAL the State (a prosecuting power) | the company and every officer in default: liability to conviction
-- src:12238 | (5) If a company makes default in complying with any requirement of this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:12239 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12240 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:12241 | This is subject to subsection (7) below.
-- src:12242 | (6) For this purpose the following are treated as officers of the company—
-- src:12243 | (a) a liquidator or administrator of the company, and
-- src:12244 | (b) a trustee of a deed for securing the issue of debentures of the company.
-- src:12245 | (7) A person is not guilty of an offence under this section if he shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests.
@ref s 897(5)-(7) Offence by the company and every officer in default; who counts as an officer; the defence (src:12238-12245)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with any requirement of section 897` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 897(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 897` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the company makes default in complying with any requirement of section 897`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with any requirement of this section, an offence is committed by"
        IF `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not guilty of an offence under this section if he shows that the default was due to the refusal"
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) any other person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the offence is committed by "(a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default": no one else is named
        OTHERWISE `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- an officer, a liquidator or administrator, or a trustee (subsection (6) treats them as officers): guilty only if in default; JUST FALSE is the "who is in default" no, supplied by s 1121

-- A defence the person must show (the 2026-11-05 ruling (b)): when it is not shown, the answer is that THIS provision gives no defence on these facts.
@ref s 897(7) The defence: refusal of a director or trustee to supply particulars (src:12245)
GIVEN `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 897(7) section 897(7) gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he shows that the default was due to the refusal" (this section gives no defence on these facts, not "no defence at all")

-- JURAL the State (a power to prosecute and the court's power to sentence) | the person guilty: liability to the penalty
-- src:12246 | (8) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:12247 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:12248 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 897(8) The penalty (src:12246-12248)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 897(8) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF mode EQUALS `on conviction on indictment`
    THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode `a fine without a stated limit`) -- "(a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine"
    ELSE JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)) -- "(b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum"

§§ `Duty of directors and trustees to provide information (s 898)`

-- JURAL the company: claim to notice of a director's or trustee's matters | any director of the company and any trustee for its debenture holders: duty to give it
-- src:12250 | (1) It is the duty of—
-- src:12251 | (a) any director of the company, and
-- src:12252 | (b) any trustee for its debenture holders,
-- src:12253 | to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as may be necessary for the purposes of section 897 (explanatory statement to be circulated or made available).
@ref s 898(1) The duty of a director or trustee to give the company notice of matters relating to himself (src:12250-12253)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of section 897` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 898(1) the person is under a duty to give the company notice of the matter` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` AND `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of section 897`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any director of the company, and any trustee for its debenture holders, to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as may be necessary"

-- JURAL the State | any person who makes default in complying with section 898: liability to conviction (s 898(2)); the penalty (s 898(3))
-- src:12254 | (2) Any person who makes default in complying with this section commits an offence.
-- src:12255 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 898(2)-(3) Offence of default and its penalty (src:12254-12255)
GIVEN `the person makes default in complying with section 898` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 898(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person makes default in complying with section 898`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who makes default in complying with this section commits an offence"

GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 898(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 897(8) the conviction is a summary conviction` mode
    THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale" says nothing of conviction on indictment

§§ `Court sanction for compromise or arrangement (s 899)`

-- 75% in value, and a majority in number: the Act says "a majority in number representing 75% in value ... present and voting".
-- JURAL the company, any creditor or member: power to apply | the court: liability to hear; the court: power to sanction | those bound: liability (s 899(1))
-- src:12258 | (1) If a majority in number representing 75% in value of the creditors or class of creditors or members or class of members (as the case may be), present and voting either in person or by proxy at the meeting summoned under section 896, agree a compromise or arrangement, the court may, on an application under this section, sanction the compromise or arrangement.
@ref s 899(1) If a majority in number representing 75% in value agree, the court may sanction (src:12258)
GIVEN `an application under section 899 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of creditors or members present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 896` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those present and voting` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those who agree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 899(1) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an application under section 899 has been made`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, on an application under this section, sanction"
        IF 2 TIMES `the number of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` GREATER THAN `the number of creditors or members present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 896`
           AND `the value represented by those who agree` AT LEAST (0.75 TIMES `the value represented by those present and voting`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a majority in number representing 75% in value of the creditors or class of creditors or members or class of members ... agree a compromise or arrangement, the court may" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F27; the count test itself is fork F2)

