GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 899(1A) section 899(1) is subject to section 899A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 899A(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 899A does not apply, and s 899(1A) says nothing else
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 899A applies is not known

-- The text shows two versions of limb (c) (lines 12263-12265); both are encoded together (fork F1): the liquidator of a company being wound up,
-- and the administrator of a company in administration or in relation to which an administration order is in force.
-- src:12260 | (2) An application under this section may be made by—
-- src:12261 | (a) the company,
-- src:12262 | (b) any creditor or member of the company,
-- src:12263 | (c) if the company is being wound up or an administration order is in force in relation it, the liquidator or administrator.
-- src:12264 | (c) if the company is being wound up, the liquidator, or
-- src:12265 | (d) if the company is in administration, the administrator.
@ref s 899(2) Who may apply for the sanction (src:12260-12265)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 896(2) applicant`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration or an administration order is in force in relation to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 896(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is being wound up, the liquidator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F28)
    WHEN `s 896(2) the administrator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is in administration or an administration order is in force in relation to it` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is in administration, the administrator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F28)
    WHEN `s 896(2) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An application under this section may be made by" lists, and does not say "only"

