GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 900(8) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 897(8) the conviction is a summary conviction` mode
    THEN JUST (`s 900(8) a penalty of a fine and a daily default fine for continued contravention` mode (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1) (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is liable on summary conviction to a fine" says nothing of conviction on indictment

§§ `Obligations of company with respect to articles etc (s 901)`

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing when the section applies)
-- src:12317 | (1) This section applies—
-- src:12318 | (a) to any order under section 899 (order sanctioning compromise or arrangement), and
-- src:12319 | (b) to any order under section 900 (order facilitating reconstruction or amalgamation) that alters the company's constitution.
@ref s 901(1) The section applies to an order under section 899 and to an order under section 900 that alters the constitution (src:12317-12319)
GIVEN `the order is an order under section 899` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901(1) this section applies to the order` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order under section 899` OR `the order is an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies— (a) to any order under section 899 ..., and (b) to any order under section 900 ... that alters the company's constitution"

-- JURAL the registrar (receipt) | the company: duty to accompany the copy of the order with the amended articles, resolution or agreement
-- src:12320 | (2) If the order amends—
-- src:12321 | (a) the company's articles, or
-- src:12322 | (b) any resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies (resolution or agreement affecting a company's constitution),
-- src:12323 | the copy of the order delivered to the registrar by the company under section 899(4) or section 900(6) must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended.
@ref s 901(2) The copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by the amended articles, resolution or agreement (src:12320-12323)
GIVEN `s 901(1) this section applies to the order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order amends the company's articles or a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy delivered to the registrar is accompanied by a copy of the articles, or the resolution or agreement, as amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901(2) the copy of the order is accompanied as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901(1) this section applies to the order`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to the order is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is in a section that applies only to the orders it names
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT (`the order amends the company's articles or a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the order amends" the articles or a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement
        ELSE IF `the copy delivered to the registrar is accompanied by a copy of the articles, or the resolution or agreement, as amended`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- JURAL anyone to whom the company issues a copy of its articles: claim to a copy of the order | the company: duty to accompany each copy of the articles
-- src:12324 | (3) Every copy of the company's articles issued by the company after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy of the order, unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment.
@ref s 901(3) Every copy of the articles issued after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy of the order (src:12324)
GIVEN `s 901(1) this section applies to the order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the articles is issued by the company after the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the articles is accompanied by a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901(3) the copy of the articles is accompanied as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 901(1) this section applies to the order`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to the order is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is in a section that applies only to the orders it names
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT (`the copy of the articles is issued by the company after the order is made`)
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every copy of the company's articles issued by the company after the order is made"
            IF `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment`
                THEN JUST TRUE -- "unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment": the exception is met, so nothing more is required and the copy is as the section requires (an "unless" once met: fork F10)
            IF `the copy of the articles is accompanied by a copy of the order`
                THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a copy of the order" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

DECLARE `s 901(4) what an article reference means` IS ONE OF
    `s 901(4)(a) a reference to the effect of the order`
    `s 901(4)(b) a reference to the articles of a company not having articles`

-- Rules of reading (s 901(4)): the second argument is what the reference points at.
-- src:12325 | (4) In this section—
-- src:12326 | (a) references to the effect of the order include the effect of the compromise or arrangement to which the order relates; and
-- src:12327 | (b) in the case of a company not having articles, references to its articles shall be read as references to the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution.
@ref s 901(4) References to the effect of the order, and to the articles of a company not having articles (src:12325-12327)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 901(4) what an article reference means`
      `the thing is the effect of the compromise or arrangement to which the order relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901(4) the thing is within the reference` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 901(4)(a) a reference to the effect of the order` THEN
        IF `the thing is the effect of the compromise or arrangement to which the order relates` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to the effect of the order include the effect of the compromise or arrangement"
    WHEN `s 901(4)(b) a reference to the articles of a company not having articles` THEN
        IF `the thing is the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a company not having articles, references to its articles shall be read as references to the instrument constituting the company or defining its constitution"

-- JURAL the State | the company and every officer in default: liability to conviction (s 901(5)); the penalty (s 901(6))
-- src:12328 | (5) If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:12329 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12330 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 901(5) Offence if a company makes default in complying with the section (src:12328-12330)
GIVEN `a company makes default in complying with section 901` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 901(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 901` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a company makes default in complying with section 901`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by"
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person EQUALS `s 897(5) any other person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the offence is committed by "(a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
        OTHERWISE `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:12331 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 901(6) The penalty: level 3 on the standard scale (src:12331)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 901(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 897(8) the conviction is a summary conviction` mode
    THEN JUST (`s 897(8) a penalty of a fine only` mode (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is liable on summary conviction to a fine" says nothing of conviction on indictment

